## Barcode classification and demultiplexing

Demultiplexing performance was summarized as the proportion of reads assigned to expected sample barcodes relative to the total number of reads subjected to barcode classification. Reads not assigned to a barcode were recorded as unclassified.

### Sequencing run 1

Barcodes 1–10 were used.

- Total reads subjected to barcode classification: 302,659
- Reads assigned to expected sample barcodes: 274,029 (90.5%)
- Unclassified reads: 28,613 (9.5%)
- Reads assigned outside the expected barcode range: 17 (<0.01%)

### Sequencing run 2

Barcodes 11–24 were used.

- Total reads subjected to barcode classification: 305,315
- Reads assigned to expected sample barcodes: 269,405 (88.2%)
- Unclassified reads: 35,564 (11.6%)
- Reads assigned outside the expected barcode range: 346 (0.1%)
